issues.body:
Fresh live portfolio reconciliation after the 2026-09-10 GitHub scan.

Current head `9065a675c1a1ba1880046bb79adfbeadffc81c91`.

Control-state reconciliation:
- replaces stale `manus-codebase` registry identity with verified `Affiliate-Websites`;
- refreshes all 10 accessible repositories to current observed default branches and public visibility;
- records all 10 as scanned in this reconciliation cycle;
- updates `.overseer/STATE.yml` from stale 2026-09-01/null-scan state to 2026-09-10 discovery/scan state;
- retains an active HIGH control-plane finding rather than manufacturing portfolio GREEN;
- declares `.overseer/PROJECT-OVERSEERS/` the only live Project Overseer control root while preserving lowercase `.overseer/project-overseers/` as historical evidence only;
- adds deterministic tests preventing canonical STATE/REGISTRY from routing through the lowercase historical tree.

Issue #42 supervision slice:
- adds a small `portfolio_health` composition layer over the existing health contract rather than a second scheduler/runtime;
- consumes explicit observed checks and canonical repository membership;
- maps access/critical failures/unknown or stale assurance to safer BLOCKED/RED/AMBER dispositions;
- routes non-GREEN findings only through a caller-supplied Project Overseer callback;
- routing itself cannot promote health;
- a deterministic fixture proves AMBER finding -> routed remediation boundary -> fresh post-remediation observation -> GREEN;
- non-canonical repositories fail closed before routing.

This is not live production orchestration and does not execute remediation, assurance or scheduling. The Green/PRS boundary remains external and independent. No project implementation is declared GREEN from this PR.

The earlier head `7bd342c...` received a successful Amazon Q review. No CI/check run has yet appeared for the current exact head; do not borrow the earlier review as current-head assurance.

No merge, approval, mark-ready, deployment, credential change, production autonomy, historical-evidence deletion or production mutation.
